---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "AI Workflow Consulting",
  "serviceType": "AI Consulting",
  "provider": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pravine Manivannan", "url": "https://pravinemani.com/" },
  "areaServed": "Worldwide",
  "description": "Production-grade AI workflows. Custom MCP servers. Agent systems. Prompt + eval suites. Built code-first on Claude Code and Vercel.",
  "url": "https://pravinemani.com/services/ai/"
};
---

<Base title="AI Workflow Consulting · Claude Code, MCP, Agents · Pravine Mani" description="Production AI workflows. Custom MCP servers. Agent systems. Eval suites. Built code-first on Claude Code and Vercel. Toronto consultancy." jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/services/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">services</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <span class="you">ai</span>
  </div>
  <h1>AI workflows.<br><span class="accent">Production-grade. Code-first.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">AI workflows shipped on a code-first stack. Claude Code. Vercel cron. MCP servers. Supabase. No n8n. No Make. No platform fee.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a href="/services/" class="cta-btn secondary">All engagement shapes</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-grid">

    <article class="vert-card" id="workflows">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">01</span><h2>Workflow automation</h2></div>
      <p>Daily briefings. Lead-routing. Inbox triage. Competitor watch. Metric digests. Any workflow with a clear input and output. Shipped as code, not strung through SaaS.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Vercel cron + serverless on your account</li>
        <li>Anthropic API with prompt caching from day one</li>
        <li>Typed outputs (Zod or Pydantic); no free-text parsing</li>
        <li>14 days of post-ship support included</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="mcp">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">02</span><h2>Custom MCP servers</h2></div>
      <p>Wrap your domain logic as a Model Context Protocol server. Claude (or any MCP-compatible agent) calls your APIs, databases, and internal tools as first-class actions.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Tool registration, Zod-validated inputs, typed errors</li>
        <li>HMAC verification on every external trigger</li>
        <li>Repo template + README + Loom handoff</li>
        <li>Pairs with custom Claude Code skills (CLI installable)</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="agents">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">03</span><h2>Agent systems</h2></div>
      <p>Multi-step agents. Tool use. Structured outputs. Sane fallbacks. Single-agent or fan-out. Live observability via Langfuse or Helicone. Cost ceilings per user.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Orchestrator / worker / evaluator patterns where they fit</li>
        <li>Sub-agent spawning when parallelism is the win</li>
        <li>Idempotency keys + exponential backoff</li>
        <li>For deeper multi-agent / concurrency work, see <a href="/services/agentic-os/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Agentic OS</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="evals">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">04</span><h2>Prompt + eval suites</h2></div>
      <p>A golden dataset of 30-100 inputs with expected outputs. Scored on every prompt change. Runs in CI. PRs that drop eval score block merge. This is the discipline that separates a demo from a product.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Promptfoo (free) or Braintrust setups</li>
        <li>Regression harness + report on every PR</li>
        <li>Prompts versioned in git like code</li>
        <li>Output: you own a real test suite, not just a working demo</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="title-block">
      <div class="label">how it works</div>
      <h2>Engagement shapes for AI work.</h2>
      <p>Same three engagement shapes across all focus areas. Full ladder and pricing brackets at <a href="/services/">/services</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="vert-engagements">
    <a href="/services/#audit" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">SYSTEM AUDIT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE WEEK · MID 4-FIG</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#sprint" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">BUILD SPRINT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE BUILD · MID 4-FIG</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#custom" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">CUSTOM BUILD</span><span class="when">QUOTE-BASED · LOW 5-FIG+</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-cta reveal" style="text-align: center;">
    <p style="margin: 0;">Working on something AI-shaped? <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Send the problem →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
